WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.220
Workstations support mission intake, flight planning, airspace and weather review,

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:07.000
communications, telemetry, data processing, mapping, and reporting.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.235
Access should match roles,

00:00:08.235 --> 00:00:12.000
and displays should emphasize actionable status rather than decorative metrics.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.700
Controllers, aircraft, payloads,

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.000
and accessories need secure labeled storage with check-in and check-out.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Physical security protects equipment, credentials, removable media,

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.180
and sensitive mission information from unauthorized use or loss.

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.740
Battery areas require approved chargers, suitable surfaces, separation,

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:31.080
condition tracking, ventilation or monitoring as appropriate,

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.980
and response procedures for abnormal batteries.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:36.000
Charging should not become an unattended background activity.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.230
Data storage should separate raw collection, working products, reports, and exports.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.350
Capacity, backup, encryption, retention,

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:47.240
and recovery must be planned before operations produce large volumes of imagery and video.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:51.965
Communications may include voice, messaging, incident channels, and contact lists.

00:00:51.965 --> 00:00:55.930
The center needs resilient methods and a clear priority order so routine updates do not

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:56.934
obscure safety calls.

00:00:56.934 --> 00:00:59.960
Record important decisions without overwhelming the crew.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:03.050
A maintenance area should support inspection, cleaning, configuration,

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:06.985
and controlled repair while preventing parts or tools from mixing across assets.

00:01:06.985 --> 00:01:09.230
Facility design should follow the workflow and hazards,

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.000
not imitate an impressive command center.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.780
Plan continuity for power loss, network outage, unavailable displays,

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:17.000
inaccessible storage, or evacuation.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.640
Crews need offline contacts, protected checklists, alternate records,

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.970
and a clear point when centralized support is no longer dependable.
